# bail-processing-algorithms

Importance Score: 85/100

The bail processing system implements specialized logic for handling bond status determination and eligibility verification:

## Bond Format Normalization (app/telnyx_tools.py)
- Converts varied bond amount formats into standardized representation
- Handles special cases like PR bonds and "no bond" designations
- Normalizes text variations for amount extraction 
- Flags cases requiring manual review when patterns are ambiguous

## Eligibility Rules Engine (app/telnyx_tools.py)
- Analyzes bond status text to determine eligibility
- Implements jurisdiction-specific rules for bond qualification
- Processes conditional bond requirements
- Identifies cases requiring human intervention
- Flags high-risk or special circumstance bonds

## Fast-Path Lookup System
- Maintains lookup tables for common bond scenarios
- Maps status codes to eligibility determination
- Provides immediate responses for standard cases
- Routes complex cases to detailed analysis pipeline

## Bond Status Categories
- Active bonds
- Denied bonds
- Pending review
- Special conditions
- Hold status
- PR bond eligible
- No bond allowed

## Primary Processing Workflow
1. Initial status text normalization
2. Fast-path lookup attempt
3. Pattern-based eligibility analysis
4. Special case detection
5. Human review flagging
6. Final status determination

